ASTRA — Autonomous Safety, Trust, and Runtime Architecture
==========================================================

Origin
------
Developed in the Department of Computer Science and Engineering, B.M.S. College
of Engineering, Bengaluru, under the guidance of Dr. Chaitra R.

Authors: Sushanth C., Tanay S. Huddar, Tarun Gowda V., T. Tilak Reddy.

Status
------
Unpublished, confidential, proprietary. See LICENSE.

An intended patent filing covers the architecture implemented here. Until that
filing is confirmed complete, this repository must remain private and must not
be demonstrated, described in detail, or distributed outside the project team
without a non-disclosure agreement in place. This mirrors the open item
recorded in the project's Prototype & Demo Plan, which gates any external or
company-facing demonstration on the filing status.

Third-party components
----------------------
This distribution contains no third-party source code. Runtime dependencies are
declared in pyproject.toml and are obtained from the Python Package Index under
their own licences. A dependency licence inventory is required before any
external distribution; it is tracked as Phase 8 work in docs/ROADMAP.md.

Safety
------
This is a research prototype and is not certified for use in any safety-related
system. See the SAFETY NOTICE in LICENSE.
